# .cursorrules — Architecture Diagram Platform

## Project overview
A C4 Model architecture diagramming platform built with React, TypeScript, Vite, and React Flow.
Think IcePanel.io — multiple independent diagrams, drill-down navigation, AWS service nodes, flows, and a service registry.

## Tech stack
- **React 18** + **TypeScript** (strict)
- **Vite** with `@vitejs/plugin-react-swc`
- **React Flow** (`@xyflow/react`) — canvas, nodes, edges
- **Zustand** + **immer** middleware — all global state
- **Tailwind CSS** — styling only, no CSS modules or inline styles
- **shadcn/ui** — UI primitives
- **lucide-react** — icons only
- **framer-motion** — transitions and panel animations
- **react-router-dom** — routing

## Project structure
```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── canvas/         # ArchCanvas, C4Node, C4Edge, PanelNode, CanvasToolbar, ElementPanel
│   └── ui/             # shadcn primitives
├── lib/
│   ├── model-store.ts  # Zustand store — single source of truth
│   ├── model-types.ts  # All TypeScript interfaces
│   ├── aws-catalog.ts  # AWS service/category definitions
│   └── github-import.ts # GitHub repo tech stack detection
├── pages/
│   ├── Dashboard.tsx   # Diagram list
│   ├── ModelExplorer.tsx # Canvas page
│   └── Index.tsx
└── hooks/
```

## Data model (model-types.ts)

### Core types
```ts
ComponentType = "person" | "system" | "container" | "component" | "panel" | AwsCategoryId

Component {
  id, name, type: ComponentType, description
  technology?: string
  parentId: string | null       // React Flow parent-child for panel grouping
  tags?: string[]
  awsService?: string           // AWS service id from aws-catalog
  serviceId?: string            // links to ServiceDefinition in registry
  linkedDiagramId?: string      // links to another Diagram for navigation
  width?: number                // panels only
  height?: number               // panels only
}

Connection { id, sourceId, targetId, label, technology?, description? }

ServiceDefinition { id, name, description, repositoryUrl, technology[], owner?, tags? }

ViewNodeLayout { elementId, x, y, zIndex? }

Diagram {
  id, name, level: Level, domain?, updatedAt
  snapshot: ModelDraft          // isolated draft per diagram
  nodeLayouts: ViewNodeLayout[]
  viewport: { x, y, zoom }
}

ModelDraft { components, connections, serviceRegistry }
```

### Planned types (not yet implemented — add when needed)
```ts
FlowStep { order, componentId?, connectionId?, note? }
Flow { id, name, mermaid, steps: FlowStep[], diagramId }
EmbeddedDiagram { id, diagramId, originComponentId, x, y, width, height }
```

## State management rules (CRITICAL)

### Always follow these patterns:
1. **All state lives in `useDiagramStore`** — no local state for data, only for UI (modals, panels open/closed)
2. **All mutations use immer** — mutate `state` directly inside `set()`
3. **Selectors that return arrays/objects MUST use `useShallow`** to prevent infinite re-render loops
4. **`useDiagramActions()`** must always use `useShallow` — it returns an object of functions
5. **Never return new arrays/objects from selectors without `useShallow`** — `Object.values()` and `.filter()` always create new references

```ts
// ✅ Correct
export const useVisibleComponents = () =>
  useDiagramStore(useShallow((s) => {
    return Object.values(s.diagrams[s.activeDiagramId!].snapshot.components).filter(...)
  }));

// ❌ Wrong — infinite loop
export const useVisibleComponents = () =>
  useDiagramStore((s) => Object.values(...).filter(...));
```

6. **Active diagram is always accessed via `activeDiagramId`** — use the `activeDiagram()` helper inside the store
7. **`serviceRegistry` is per-diagram** — lives inside `diagram.snapshot.serviceRegistry`, not global

## Canvas rules (React Flow)

### Node types registered in ArchCanvas:
```ts
const nodeTypes = { c4: C4Node, panel: PanelNode };
const edgeTypes = { c4: C4Edge };
```

### Node rendering order — panels MUST come first:
```ts
const sorted = [...visibleComponents].sort((a, b) =>
  a.type === "panel" ? -1 : b.type === "panel" ? 1 : 0
);
```

### Panel nodes use parent-child system:
- `parentId` on a Component → set as `parentId` on the React Flow node
- `extent: "parent"` on children inside panels
- `zIndex: -1` for panels, `zIndex: 1` for regular nodes

### Handles are horizontal:
- `type="target"` → `Position.Left`
- `type="source"` → `Position.Right`

### Edges are straight lines:
- Use `getStraightPath` from `@xyflow/react` (not getBezierPath)
- `sourcePosition` and `targetPosition` are NOT passed to `getStraightPath`

### Viewport persistence:
- Use `onMoveEnd` (not `onMove`) to call `updateViewport` — avoids re-render loop

### `onNodeDragStop` detects panel drops:
```ts
// When a non-panel node is dropped inside a panel boundary → setParent(nodeId, panelId)
// When dropped outside all panels → setParent(nodeId, null)
```

## Component conventions

### Selectors to use in components:
```ts
useActiveDiagram()          // full Diagram object
useComponents()             // Record<string, Component>
useComponent(id)            // single Component
useConnections()            // Record<string, Connection>
useVisibleComponents()      // Component[] filtered by nodeLayouts
useVisibleConnections()     // Connection[] filtered by visible node ids
useAllDiagrams()            // Diagram[] for dashboard list
useServiceRegistry()        // Record<string, ServiceDefinition>
useAllServices()            // ServiceDefinition[]
useDiagramActions()         // all actions — always useShallow
```

### Actions available via `useDiagramActions()`:
```ts
// Diagrams
addDiagram(name, level, domain?)
openDiagram(id)
deleteDiagram(id)

// Components
addComponent(type, name, parentId, position?, awsService?)
updateComponent(id, patch)
removeComponent(id)          // also removes children and their connections

// Connections
addConnection(sourceId, targetId, label)
updateConnection(id, patch)
removeConnection(id)

// Layout
updateNodeLayout(elementId, position)
updateViewport(viewport)
bringToFront(elementId)
sendToBack(elementId)

// Service registry
addService(service)
updateService(id, patch)
removeService(id)
linkComponentToService(componentId, serviceId | undefined)
linkComponentToDiagram(componentId, diagramId | undefined)
```

## Key behaviors

### Navigation between diagrams:
- `Dashboard` lists all diagrams → click row → `openDiagram(id)` → navigate to `/model/:id`
- `ModelExplorer` reads `useActiveDiagram()`

### Linked diagram navigation:
- If `component.linkedDiagramId` is set → "Explorar interior" button calls `openDiagram(linkedDiagramId)` and navigates
- If not set → no drill-down (drill-down navigation was removed in favor of separate diagrams)

### AWS nodes:
- `isAwsType(type)` from `aws-catalog.ts` detects AWS category types
- `AWS_SERVICE_MAP`, `AWS_CATEGORY_MAP` for icon/name lookup
- `AwsIcon` component lazy-loads icons via `import("aws-react-icons")` — lib is CJS, pre-bundled via `optimizeDeps.include` in vite.config.ts

### Panel nodes:
- `type: "panel"` — resizable container, no handles, no connections
- Uses `NodeResizer` from `@reactflow/node-resizer`
- `width`/`height` stored on `Component`, passed as `style` to React Flow node
- `onResize` → `updateComponent(id, { width, height })`

### Z-order:
- `bringToFront` → `zIndex = max + 1`
- `sendToBack` → `zIndex = min - 1`
- `zIndex` stored in `ViewNodeLayout`, not in `Component`

## Styling conventions
- Dark theme — `bg-card`, `bg-background`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`
- Node colors by type: `text-node-person`, `text-node-system`, `text-node-container`, `text-node-component`
- AWS category colors: `text-aws-compute`, `border-aws-storage/50`, etc.
- Never use inline styles except for dynamic values (position, size)
- Never use CSS modules
- Tailwind utility classes only

## What NOT to do
- Never add `Provider` wrappers for data — Zustand needs no provider
- Never use `useCallback` with `draft` as dependency — use store actions instead
- Never call `Object.values()` in a selector without `useShallow`
- Never use `getBezierPath` — edges are straight (`getStraightPath`)
- Never use `onMove` for viewport — use `onMoveEnd`
- Never put playback/flow state in the Zustand store — keep it in local `useState`
- Never render Mermaid as a diagram — only parse it as text for flows
- Never add `parentId` to panel nodes themselves
